KG42.register("rules-f558731251df501c098da8ec",{"id":"46-commercial_building_transactive_control::v141-c-R006","paper":"46-commercial_building_transactive_control","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R006","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local market clearing","process_stage":"clearing","market_meaning":"Demand curves specifying requested quantities at different prices are horizontally aggregated and used in market clearing. Scope: Air, water and electricity markets within central-HVAC transactive control. Supply curves specifying offered quantities at different prices provide inputs to clearing their corresponding markets. Scope: Air, water and electricity markets within central-HVAC transactive control.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function clearing.local under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.demand","bidding.supply","clearing.local"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R006-E001","source":"bidding.demand","target":"clearing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R006-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"clearing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e08"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Air, water and electricity markets within central-HVAC transactive control.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e08"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Demand curves specifying requested quantities at different prices are horizontally aggregated and used in market clearing. Scope: Air, water and electricity markets within central-HVAC transactive control.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Supply curves specifying offered quantities at different prices provide inputs to clearing their corresponding markets. Scope: Air, water and electricity markets within central-HVAC transactive control.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e08"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Let \\mathcal{D} be the set of demand curves in one market, where each D(p) gives the requested quantity at price p, and let S(p) give the seller's offered quantity at price p. The clearing price p^{*} is a price at which the single supply curve intersects the horizontally aggregated demand curve: S(p^{*}) = \\sum_{D \\in \\mathcal{D}} D(p^{*}). Scope: Air, water and electricity markets within central-HVAC transactive control; this formalizes the intersection case only.","expression":"p^{*} \\in \\left\\{ p \\mid S(p) = \\sum_{D \\in \\mathcal{D}} D(p) \\right\\}","formalization_origin":"equivalent_translation","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","bidding.supply","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e08"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-0abd014fd6-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 4. Market cleari buyer is willing to purchase under different prices. Likewise, the supply curv","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Each market consists of several demand curves and one supply curve. A demand curve describes the quantity of the commodity each buyer is willing to purchase under different prices. Likewise, the supply curve describes the quantity of the commodity the seller is willing to sell under different prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e06","location":{"location_id":"src-0abd014fd6-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 4. Market cleari buyer is willing to purchase under different prices. Likewise, the supply curv","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 4","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"As illustrated in Fig. 4, each market is cleared by (1) horizontally aggregating the demand curves and then (2) finding the intersection between the supply curve and the aggregated demand curves."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e08","location":{"location_id":"src-0abd014fd6-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 5 describes execution of the market-based control, which com- prises three steps: • Step 1: Dem","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Step 2: Market Clearing\nThis step clears all the markets with the corresponding supply curves. The supply curve of the electricity market is determined based on the objective of the DR services (examples are provided in Section 4). For the water market and the air markets, the supply curves are generated based on the clearing electricity price. In this case, those supply curves are “flat”, meaning the commodity is sold at a constant price regardless of the quantity, when the quantity is less than a capacity limit. When the quantity is larger than the capacity limit, those supply curves are “vertical”, meaning the commodity is sold at a constant quantity regardless of the price."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"The clearing evidence defines curve-valued inputs and a price at which curves intersect, but it does not define scalar design or operational decision variables with symbols and domains for this rule. The p in C003 is a bound price used to define the clearing-price set, not an exogenously selected x.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed constants, coefficients, capacity limits, or numeric parameter values are stated in this rule's clearing evidence. Supply-curve shape and capacity-limit details belong to the separate supply-submission rule, not to this clearing rule."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","quote":"A demand curve describes the quantity of the commodity each buyer is willing to purchase under different prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e06","quote":"each market is cleared by (1) horizontally aggregating the demand curves and then (2) finding the intersection between the supply curve and the aggregated demand curves."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","quote":"Likewise, the supply curve describes the quantity of the commodity the seller is willing to sell under different prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e08","quote":"This step clears all the markets with the corresponding supply curves."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"f854cba28167ca50098bd50c8efa8a7bf59db6ea8ab5d898b2d458065b26dce6","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The supplied evidence supports a formal clearing statement: each market has several price-quantity demand curves and one supply curve; clearing horizontally aggregates the demand curves and finds the intersection with the supply curve. C003 captures this as equality between supplied quantity and summed demanded quantity at the clearing price. The original C.1 procedural constraints C001 and C002 are retained unchanged. No no-intersection fallback, tie-break, domain, numeric parameter, or supply-curve capacity detail is added. B evidence remains unreviewed under the experiment policy; this is not a claim of independent source review.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","node_ids":["bidding.demand","clearing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R006-E001"],"rationale":"Preserves the C.1 procedural demand-side constraint. It links the demand curves produced in bidding.demand to clearing.local through E001; no separate scalar x/theta is introduced because the evidence defines curve-valued objects rather than scalar decision variables."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","node_ids":["bidding.supply","clearing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R006-E002"],"rationale":"Preserves the C.1 procedural supply-side constraint. It links the supply curve produced in bidding.supply to clearing.local through E002; no separate scalar x/theta is introduced."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C003","node_ids":["bidding.demand","bidding.supply","clearing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R006-E001","v141-c-R006-E002"],"rationale":"Formalizes the joint clearing step. The demand curves from bidding.demand enter clearing.local via E001; the single supply curve from bidding.supply enters via E002. 'Horizontally aggregating the demand curves' is translated as summing requested quantities at a common price p over the market's set of demand curves; 'finding the intersection' is translated as equality between the supply quantity and that aggregated demand quantity. This is an explicitly justified equivalent formalization of the stated aggregation-then-intersection procedure; no no-intersection fallback, tie-break, domain, or numeric parameter is added."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
